          "name": "What is halfvec in pgvector and how does it save RAM?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "halfvec is a native 16-bit floating-point vector data type introduced in pgvector 0.7.0. It halves the memory consumption of vector embeddings from 4 bytes per dimension (fp32) to 2 bytes (fp16), cutting PostgreSQL shared_buffers requirements and HNSW index sizes by exactly 50% with zero measurable loss in retrieval recall (recall@10 > 99.8%)."
          }
